From: baseband lane
Subject: 0541 pandora_pas: one metadata slot per pas, and release every slot for it

The 16-slot table at the top of pandora_pas.c keeps a metadata blob and its SHM bridge alive between
INIT_IMAGE and AUTH_AND_RESET.  Two lines in it disagreed with each other:

  pas_meta_hold()    took the first free slot without checking whether this pas already held one
  pas_meta_release() freed the first matching slot and returned

So loading the same image twice in one boot -- which the probes do deliberately, and which a retry
after a failed auth does -- took two slots and freed one, leaking a blob and a TrustZone bridge every
time.  After sixteen the table was full, and pas_meta_hold()'s "no slot" path released the new metadata
immediately, so the next INIT_IMAGE was handed nothing and the load failed for a reason that had
nothing to do with the load.

Now a slot for this pas is reused, and released first, which is also the only safe order: TrustZone has
to be told to forget the old blob before the memory under it is freed.  The release walks every slot
rather than stopping at the first.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
index ceb1dcc..f2c1e8c 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
@@ -70,9 +70,24 @@ struct pas_meta {
 };
 static struct pas_meta pas_meta[PAS_META_SLOTS];
 
+static void
+pas_meta_release(unsigned pas);
+
+/*
+ * One slot per pas.
+ *
+ * This used to take the first free slot without looking for one already held for the same pas, and
+ * pas_meta_release() freed only the first match.  Loading the same image twice in one boot -- which
+ * the probes do on purpose, and which a retry after a failed auth also does -- therefore took two
+ * slots and leaked one, and after sixteen the "no slot" path below released the new metadata
+ * immediately, so the next INIT_IMAGE was handed nothing.  A slot for this pas is now reused: the old
+ * one is released first, which is also the only safe order, because TrustZone must be told to forget
+ * the old blob before the memory behind it is freed.
+ */
 static void
 pas_meta_hold(unsigned pas, vm_offset_t md, uint64_t size, uint64_t bridge)
 {
+	pas_meta_release(pas);
 	for (unsigned i = 0; i < PAS_META_SLOTS; i++) {
 		if (!pas_meta[i].used) {
 			pas_meta[i].used = true;
@@ -89,7 +104,7 @@ pas_meta_hold(unsigned pas, vm_offset_t md, uint64_t size, uint64_t bridge)
 	kmem_free(kernel_map, md, (vm_size_t)size);
 }
 
-/* Frees the metadata of pas -- only after INIT_IMAGE has been told to forget it. */
+/* Frees every metadata slot held for pas -- only after INIT_IMAGE has been told to forget it. */
 static void
 pas_meta_release(unsigned pas)
 {
@@ -99,7 +114,6 @@ pas_meta_release(unsigned pas)
 			pas_meta[i].bridge = 0;
 			kmem_free(kernel_map, pas_meta[i].md, (vm_size_t)pas_meta[i].size);
 			pas_meta[i].used = false;
-			return;
 		}
 	}
 }
